.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a \f[CR]malloc\f[R]\(cqd buffer containing the decoded bytes on
success.
\f[CR]*out_len\f[R] is set to the number of decoded bytes.
The buffer has an extra NUL byte at \f[CR]buffer[*out_len]\f[R] for
convenience.
.PP
The caller must free the buffer with \f[CR]bc_free(3)\f[R].
.PP
Returns \f[B]NULL\f[R] on error (invalid input or allocation failure).
\f[CR]*out_len\f[R] is set to 0 on error.
.SH ERRORS
Returns NULL when:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]encoded\f[R] is NULL.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]out_len\f[R] is NULL.
.IP \(bu 2
The input contains invalid base64 characters.
.IP \(bu 2
